{"id":"u-767bef23-a55f-4857-b3d5-5d8ae5b46174","src":"community","title":"The Needle Mover","author":"Dario","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ReNHa9-the-needle-mover","desc":"Strength + hypertrophy for intermediate lifters, using an Upper/Lower split over 8 weeks with linear double progression and a deload in week 5. The exercise selection is grounded in what people actually report changing their physique.\n\nHow to Progress\n\nThis program uses double progression: work within a rep range. When you hit the top of the range on all sets, add weight next session. Small jumps beat missed reps.\n\n- Upper body compounds (bench, OHP, rows): +2.5 kg when you complete all sets at top of range\n- Lower body compounds (deadlift, squat, RDL, BSS): +5 kg when you complete all sets at top of range\n- Isolations: +1–2.5 kg when you hit the top of the range cleanly\n- Week 5 is a deload — drop all weights by 40%, cut sets to 2 per exercise, focus on form\n- Weeks 6–8 pick back up heavier than where you left off in week 4\n- AMRAP sets: log the rep count every week and aim to beat it\n- RPE (Rate of Perceived Exertion) targets below; these govern how hard each set should feel, not just the weight on the bar\n\nDeload Rules\n40% reduction in load. 2 sets per exercise. Same days, same exercises.\n- Run the same A/B/D/E template\n- Drop every working weight by 40%\n- Cut to 2 sets per exercise (no AMRAP sets)\n- Rest 90 seconds across the board\n- Focus on technique, mind-muscle connection, no grinding\n- Come back week 6 heavier than your week 4 top sets\n\nWK 6–8\n- Push Heavier\n- Start 5–10% above week 4 peaks. Continue double progression.\n\nIntensification Notes\n- Same program structure as weeks 1–4\n- Week 6: start 5–10% above your week 4 working weights\n- Week 7: keep adding per the standard progression rules\n- Week 8: attempt new rep PRs on all AMRAP sets\n- After week 8, either repeat the cycle or move to a more advanced program","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["M